-- The GM's quest skip (Kiciamol, 15-16 October): F9's "Misje", the target
-- board's "Misje" and the panel's "Misje graczy" (gm_quest_admin.lua,
-- gm_quest_full_skip.lua and the generated gm_quest_catalog.lua, libs/other).
-- The core's own timer reads the queue (player.web_quest_admin_actions); a
-- character's own two-second timer carries out what is queued for it - and a
-- bot's descriptor has none, so nothing queued by F9 for a bot ever runs.
-- Iwakura's Patch 20, 4J: the panel's "Zakoncz" for a bot of the population is
-- a row of source 'panel_bot' and a QUESTDONE row the bot's core serves: the
-- core marks the action in the bot's flags and fires qa_bot.timer for it once
-- (playerbot_admin_grants.h), the same execution as a person's. "/gm_quests"
-- is the F9 page's command. At every login the flags a plan's end sets are put
-- right for a character a skip ended a quest for (repair_unlocks, issue #48).
quest gm_quest_admin begin
	state start begin
		when login begin
			if gm_quest_admin_lib.armed ~= true then
				gm_quest_admin_lib.armed = true
				server_loop_timer("qa_core", 5, 0)
			end
			-- Issue #48: the flags a skip before the fix left unset (the
			-- Fisherman's introduction), put right without a second reward.
			gm_quest_admin_lib.repair_unlocks()
			if not pc.is_playerbot() then
				loop_timer("qa_player", 2)
			end
		end
		when qa_core.server_timer begin
			-- NO pc.*, pc.select or player context in this handler.
			gm_quest_admin_lib.poll()
		end
		when qa_player.timer begin
			gm_quest_admin_lib.apply_pending()
		end
		when qa_bot.timer begin
			gm_quest_admin_lib.apply_bot()
		end
		when write with mes.get_message() == "gm_quests" begin
			gm_quest_admin_lib.command(mes.get_arguments())
		end
	end
end
